<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basque Nationalist Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1895</span> · Also known as PNV, EAJ-PNV, Euzko Alderdi Jeltzalea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Basque Nationalist Party is a Christian democratic party founded in 1895 by Sabino Arana to defend Basque identity and self-government. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-civil-war">Spanish Civil War</a> it sided with the Republic in return for autonomy, and its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-antonio-aguirre">José Antonio Aguirre</a> headed the Basque government of 1936–1937 and then a government in exile. It has led the Basque autonomous government for most of the period since 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basque-nationalist-party.jpg" alt="Basque Nationalist Party" width="320" height="279" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Euzko Alderdi Jeltzalea-Partido Nacionalista Vasco · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_PNV_2025.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
